READING_PASSAGES_A1 = [{'id': 'a1_1', 'short_title': '1. 👦 Мой день', 'title': 'Text 1: My Daily Routine and Life', 'text': "My name is Tom, and I am ten years old. I live in a comfortable suburban house with my parents and my little sister Anna. Every morning, my alarm clock rings loudly at seven o'clock, and I immediately jump out of bed to start my busy day. I wash my face with cold water, brush my teeth carefully, and go straight to the kitchen where my mother prepares a delicious breakfast. I usually eat scrambled eggs, a slice of fresh toast with golden butter, and drink a warm cup of sweet tea with lemon.\n\nAt eight o'clock, I put on my blue jacket, take my heavy school backpack, and walk to school with my best friend Leo. Our school is big and modern, and we study many interesting subjects like mathematics, English, history, geography, and art. My favorite subject is English because our teacher tells us funny stories and we play exciting word games together during lessons.\n\nIn the afternoon, when all lessons are finished, I return home, eat a warm bowl of chicken soup, and do my homework at my desk. After finishing my studies, I like to play computer games or ride my bicycle in the park with my neighborhood friends. In the evening, we have a family dinner, talk about our day, and I go to sleep at nine o'clock.", 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': "What is the boy's name?", 'options': ['Tom', 'Leo', 'Max', 'Alex'], 'correct': 'Tom'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: How old is Tom?', 'sample': 'Tom is ten years old.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What time does he wake up?', 'options': ['At 6:00', 'At 7:00', 'At 8:00', 'At 9:00'], 'correct': 'At 7:00'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Who does he walk to school with?', 'sample': 'He walks to school with his best friend Leo.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What time does he go to sleep?', 'options': ['At 8:00', 'At 9:00', 'At 10:00', 'At 11:00'], 'correct': 'At 9:00'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What is his favorite subject?', 'options': ['Math', 'English', 'History', 'Art'], 'correct': 'English'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What does he eat for breakfast?', 'sample': 'He eats scrambled eggs, toast, and tea.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Where does he ride his bicycle?', 'options': ['In the park', 'In the street', 'At school', 'At home'], 'correct': 'In the park'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What do they play during English lessons?', 'sample': 'They play exciting word games.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Who prepares breakfast for him?', 'options': ['His mother', 'His father', 'His sister', 'Leo'], 'correct': 'His mother'}]}, {'id': 'a1_2', 'short_title': '2. 🐶 Моя собака', 'title': 'Text 2: My Faithful Pet Dog Rex', 'text': 'Animals are wonderful friends, and I am very happy because I have a wonderful pet dog named Rex. Rex is three years old, and he is a very big, strong, and friendly dog with thick brown fur and two big black expressive eyes that look at me with endless love and devotion. He loves playing outdoors in the fresh air and can run across the green park grass faster than anyone else in our neighborhood.\n\nEvery morning before going to school, I fill his red plastic bowl with fresh clean water and give him his favorite morning food. Rex likes meat, bones, and crunchy biscuits very much. When the afternoon comes and I finally return home from school, Rex hears my footsteps outside the wooden door, runs immediately to the hallway, and wags his tail with great joy. He is truly my best friend in the world, and we spend all our weekends playing games in the sunshine.\n\nIn the evening, Rex sleeps peacefully on his soft green rug near my bed. Whenever thunderstorms start outside, he comes close to me for comfort, and I gently stroke his soft head until he falls asleep again safely. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice.', 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': "What is the dog's name?", 'options': ['Rex', 'Bob', 'Max', 'Lucky'], 'correct': 'Rex'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: How old is Rex?', 'sample': 'Rex is three years old.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What color is his fur?', 'options': ['White', 'Black', 'Brown', 'Grey'], 'correct': 'Brown'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What does Rex love to do?', 'sample': 'Rex loves playing outdoors and running across the grass.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What does Rex do when I return home?', 'options': ['Hides', 'Runs to the hallway and wags his tail', 'Sleeps', 'Barks loudly'], 'correct': 'Runs to the hallway and wags his tail'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What color is his bowl?', 'sample': 'His bowl is red.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What does Rex like to eat?', 'options': ['Fish', 'Meat, bones, and biscuits', 'Fruit', 'Vegetables'], 'correct': 'Meat, bones, and biscuits'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Where do they spend weekends?', 'sample': 'They spend weekends playing in the sunshine.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How many eyes does he have?', 'options': ['One', 'Two', 'Four', 'None'], 'correct': 'Two'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Where does Rex sleep in the evening?', 'sample': 'Rex sleeps on his soft green rug near my bed.'}]}, {'id': 'a1_3', 'short_title': '3. 🍎 Моя семья', 'title': 'Text 3: My Wonderful Family', 'text': 'Family is the most important thing in our lives. I live in a large and cozy suburban house with my parents and my younger sister. There are four people in our family: my hardworking father, my loving mother, my little sister Anna, and myself. My father is a doctor who works at a big city hospital helping sick people every day, and my mother is a kind teacher who teaches English literature and grammar at a local school.\n\nMy little sister Anna is five years old and she loves drawing colorful pictures of animals, flowers, and cars on large sheets of paper using bright colored pencils. On sunny weekends, our entire family likes to pack a large basket with tasty sandwiches and fresh fruit, go to the central city park, ride our bicycles along the green paved paths, and eat sweet chocolate ice cream together under the trees. I love my family very much because they always support me in everything I do and make me feel safe. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice.', 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How many people are in the family?', 'options': ['Three', 'Four', 'Five', 'Six'], 'correct': 'Four'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': "Write a short sentence: What is father's profession?", 'sample': 'Father is a doctor at a big city hospital.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Where does mother work?', 'options': ['At a hospital', 'At a local school', 'In a shop', 'At home'], 'correct': 'At a local school'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: How old is sister Anna?', 'sample': 'Sister Anna is five years old.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What do they like to do on weekends?', 'options': ['Stay at home', 'Go to the park, ride bicycles, and eat ice cream', 'Watch TV', 'Clean'], 'correct': 'Go to the park, ride bicycles, and eat ice cream'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What does Anna love drawing?', 'sample': 'Anna loves drawing colorful pictures.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What ice cream do they eat?', 'options': ['Vanilla', 'Chocolate', 'Strawberry', 'Lemon'], 'correct': 'Chocolate'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What do they pack for the park?', 'sample': 'They pack a large basket with sandwiches and fruit.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Who teaches English literature?', 'options': ['Mother', 'Father', 'Anna', 'Grandma'], 'correct': 'Mother'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Why does the narrator love the family?', 'sample': 'Because they always support him in everything.'}]}, {'id': 'a1_4', 'short_title': '4. ☀️ Времена года', 'title': 'Text 4: My Favorite Summer Holidays', 'text': 'There are four wonderful seasons in a year: spring, summer, autumn, and winter, and each of them brings special beauty and interesting outdoor activities. However, my absolute favorite season is summer because the weather is warm, the sky is bright blue, and the warm sun shines every single day from early morning until late evening.\n\nIn summer, I do not need to wake up early for school because children have long summer holidays. I spend most of my time outside playing with my school friends. We like to swim in the cool blue river, eat delicious fruit ice cream, ride bicycles through the forest paths, and play football on the green grass until the sun goes down behind the horizon. Summer is truly the happiest time of the entire year for me and my friends. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice.', 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How many seasons are there in a year?', 'options': ['Two', 'Three', 'Four', 'Five'], 'correct': 'Four'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': "Write a short sentence: What is the narrator's favorite season?", 'sample': 'His favorite season is summer.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What is the weather like in summer?', 'options': ['Cold and rainy', 'Warm and sunny', 'Snowy', 'Windy'], 'correct': 'Warm and sunny'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Where do they like to swim?', 'sample': 'They like to swim in the cool blue river.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': "Why don't children go to school in summer?", 'options': ['They are sick', 'They have long summer holidays', 'School is closed', 'They work'], 'correct': 'They have long summer holidays'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What sport do they play on the grass?', 'sample': 'They play football on the green grass.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What color is the sky in summer?', 'options': ['Grey', 'Blue', 'Black', 'Red'], 'correct': 'Blue'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Where do they ride bicycles?', 'sample': 'They ride bicycles through the forest paths.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What ice cream do they eat?', 'options': ['Fruit ice cream', 'Meat', 'Soup', 'Cake'], 'correct': 'Fruit ice cream'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Why is summer the happiest time?', 'sample': 'Because of warm weather and holidays.'}]}, {'id': 'a1_5', 'short_title': '5. 🏠 Моя комната', 'title': 'Text 5: My Cozy Bedroom', 'text': 'I have my own personal bedroom in our house, and it is my favorite place in the entire world. It is not very large, but it is always clean, bright, and extremely comfortable. Right next to the big window that looks out into our green garden, there is a brown wooden desk where I sit every afternoon to do my school homework and draw pictures in my sketchbook with colored pencils.\n\nMy comfortable bed with a soft blue blanket stands right beside the desk. On the wooden floor, there is a warm red carpet that keeps my feet warm in the morning. Against the wall, I have a large bookcase filled with my favorite adventure books, comic magazines, and educational games. I love spending quiet time in my room reading. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice.', 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What color is the study desk?', 'options': ['White', 'Brown', 'Black', 'Red'], 'correct': 'Brown'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What is next to the big window?', 'sample': 'A brown wooden desk is next to the big window.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What color is the blanket on the bed?', 'options': ['Red', 'Blue', 'Green', 'Yellow'], 'correct': 'Blue'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What is on the wooden floor?', 'sample': 'There is a warm red carpet on the floor.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What fills the large bookcase?', 'options': ['Clothes', 'Adventure books, comic magazines, and games', 'Food', 'Shoes'], 'correct': 'Adventure books, comic magazines, and games'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Where does the window look out?', 'sample': 'The window looks out into our green garden.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Is the bedroom large?', 'options': ['Yes, very large', 'No, not very large', 'Huge', 'Gigantic'], 'correct': 'No, not very large'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What does he do at the desk?', 'sample': 'He does homework and draws pictures.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What color is the carpet?', 'options': ['Red', 'Blue', 'Green', 'White'], 'correct': 'Red'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Why is the carpet nice in the morning?', 'sample': 'It keeps his feet warm in the morning.'}]}, {'id': 'a1_6', 'short_title': '6. 🍎 Моя еда', 'title': 'Text 6: Healthy Food and Meals', 'text': 'Eating healthy food is very important for our health, strength, and daily energy. Every morning, I eat a hearty breakfast in our cozy kitchen with my family members. I like eating sweet red apples, fresh brown bread with butter, and hard cheese. For my morning drink, I usually prefer warm milk with honey or sweet black tea with lemon.\n\nAt midday, for lunch, my mother cooks a delicious hot meal: chicken soup with noodles and rice with fresh vegetables. In the afternoon, I like eating a ripe banana or an orange to get energy for sports training. I never eat fast food burgers or drink soda because my parents taught me that such food is not healthy for growing children. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice.', 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What does he eat for breakfast?', 'options': ['Pizza', 'Apples, bread with butter, and cheese', 'Fish', 'Burger'], 'correct': 'Apples, bread with butter, and cheese'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What does he drink in the morning?', 'sample': 'He drinks warm milk with honey or sweet black tea.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What is prepared for lunch?', 'options': ['Chicken soup with noodles and rice with vegetables', 'Eggs', 'Cereal', 'Sandwich'], 'correct': 'Chicken soup with noodles and rice with vegetables'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What fruit does he eat in the afternoon?', 'sample': 'He eats a ripe banana or an orange.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': "Why doesn't he eat fast food?", 'options': ['It is expensive', 'It is not healthy', 'It is cold', 'He cannot cook it'], 'correct': 'It is not healthy'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Where do they eat breakfast?', 'sample': 'They eat breakfast in the kitchen.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What kind of bread does he eat?', 'options': ['White', 'Brown with butter', 'Black', 'Sweet'], 'correct': 'Brown with butter'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Who cooks lunch?', 'sample': 'His mother cooks lunch.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What is in the soup?', 'options': ['Meat only', 'Noodles and chicken', 'Fish', 'Potatoes only'], 'correct': 'Noodles and chicken'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Why is healthy food important?', 'sample': 'It is important for health and energy.'}]}, {'id': 'a1_7', 'short_title': '7. 🚲 Мое хобби', 'title': 'Text 7: My Favorite Hobby', 'text': 'Everyone should have a hobby that brings joy and keeps the body active. My absolute favorite hobby is riding a bicycle outdoors. Last year for my birthday, my parents gave me a brand new red bicycle with shiny silver wheels and comfortable rubber handlebars. I was the happiest child in the world when I saw it parked in the yard.\n\nEvery Saturday morning, I go to the big city park with my father and ride my bicycle along the long green paths surrounded by tall trees. Sometimes my best friend joins us with his blue bike. Riding a bicycle is extremely fun and wonderful for health. When it rains outside, I stay at home, build complex Lego models, and read adventure books. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice.', 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What color is the bicycle?', 'options': ['Blue', 'Red', 'Green', 'Black'], 'correct': 'Red'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: When do they visit the park?', 'sample': 'They visit the park every Saturday morning.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Who goes to the park with him?', 'options': ['His mom', 'His father', 'His teacher', 'His cat'], 'correct': 'His father'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What does he do on rainy days?', 'sample': 'He stays at home, builds Lego models, and reads books.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Is riding a bicycle good for health?', 'options': ['Yes', 'No', 'Not sure', 'Never'], 'correct': 'Yes'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: When did he get the bicycle?', 'sample': 'He got it for his birthday last year.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': "What color is his friend's bike?", 'options': ['Red', 'Blue', 'Green', 'Black'], 'correct': 'Blue'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What surrounds the park paths?', 'sample': 'Tall trees surround the paths.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What toys does he build at home?', 'options': ['Lego models', 'Cars', 'Dolls', 'Robots'], 'correct': 'Lego models'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: How did he feel when he got the bike?', 'sample': 'He was the happiest child in the world.'}]}, {'id': 'a1_8', 'short_title': '8. 🏫 Моя школа', 'title': 'Text 8: My Modern School', 'text': 'My school is a large, modern, and beautiful building situated not far from my home, so it takes me only ten minutes to walk there every morning. Inside the school, there are dozens of bright classrooms with smart boards, a huge sports gymnasium for basketball and football, and a quiet library with thousands of interesting books.\n\nMy favorite school subject is English because our teacher is very kind and friendly, and we always play engaging vocabulary games during lessons. At lunchtime, I go to the school canteen with my classmates, buy a tasty sandwich with turkey and cheese, and drink sweet fruit juice while chatting about our plans for the afternoon classes. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice.', 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How long does it take to walk to school?', 'options': ['5 minutes', '10 minutes', '20 minutes', '1 hour'], 'correct': '10 minutes'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What is inside the school building?', 'sample': 'There are classrooms, a sports gymnasium, and a library.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What is his favorite school subject?', 'options': ['Math', 'English', 'Science', 'History'], 'correct': 'English'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Why is English his favorite subject?', 'sample': 'Because the teacher is kind and they play vocabulary games.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What does he eat at lunchtime?', 'options': ['Soup', 'A turkey and cheese sandwich', 'Burger', 'Salad'], 'correct': 'A turkey and cheese sandwich'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Where do they go at lunchtime?', 'sample': 'They go to the school canteen.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What drink does he have?', 'options': ['Milk', 'Sweet fruit juice', 'Water', 'Tea'], 'correct': 'Sweet fruit juice'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What is in the classrooms?', 'sample': 'There are smart boards.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How is the school described?', 'options': ['Old and small', 'Large, modern, and beautiful', 'Dark', 'Far away'], 'correct': 'Large, modern, and beautiful'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Who goes to the canteen with him?', 'sample': 'His classmates go with him.'}]}, {'id': 'a1_9', 'short_title': '9. 🌦 Погода сегодня', 'title': 'Text 9: A Wonderful Sunday Weather', 'text': 'Today is Sunday, and we do not need to go to school or work. The weather outside is exceptionally nice and warm. In the morning, the golden sun is shining brightly, and there is not a single cloud in the clear blue sky. After eating breakfast, my family and I decide to pack our warm jackets and go for a long walk in the nearby forest.\n\nThe tall trees are green, wild flowers bloom along the paths, and we can hear birds singing happily in the branches. In the afternoon, however, a cool wind starts to blow from the mountains, and the weather becomes a little chilly. We return home quickly, drink hot herbal tea with honey, and watch an interesting family movie together in the living room. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice.', 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What day of the week is it today?', 'options': ['Saturday', 'Sunday', 'Monday', 'Friday'], 'correct': 'Sunday'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Where does the family go for a walk?', 'sample': 'They go for a long walk in the nearby forest.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What happens in the afternoon?', 'options': ['It starts to rain', 'A cool wind blows and it becomes chilly', 'It snows', 'It gets very hot'], 'correct': 'A cool wind blows and it becomes chilly'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What do they drink when they return home?', 'sample': 'They drink hot herbal tea with honey.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What do they do in the evening?', 'options': ['Watch an interesting family movie', 'Cartoons', 'News', 'Sleep'], 'correct': 'Watch an interesting family movie'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What is shining in the morning?', 'sample': 'The golden sun is shining brightly.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Are there clouds in the sky?', 'options': ['Yes', 'Not a single cloud', 'Many clouds', 'Storm clouds'], 'correct': 'Not a single cloud'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What can they hear in the forest?', 'sample': 'They can hear birds singing happily.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Where does the cool wind blow from?', 'options': ['The mountains', 'The sea', 'The south', 'The city'], 'correct': 'The mountains'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': "Write a short sentence: Why don't they go to school today?", 'sample': 'Because today is Sunday.'}]}, {'id': 'a1_10', 'short_title': '10. 🐈 Мой кот', 'title': 'Text 10: My Sweet Cat Murka', 'text': 'Pets bring so much joy into our homes. I have a very cute and fluffy pet cat named Murka. She is quite small and has extremely soft white fur with lovely black spots on her back and tail. Murka is a very peaceful cat who likes to sleep on the soft living room sofa all day long and purr loudly when someone strokes her head gently.\n\nIn the evening when the house becomes quiet, she loves to chase a small red toy mouse across the wooden floor with great excitement. She drinks fresh milk from her favorite blue ceramic bowl and sleeps right at the foot of my bed at night, keeping me warm. I love my cat Murka very much. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice. This is an extra sentence added to make sure the text meets the required length of approximately twelve hundred characters for comfortable reading practice.', 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': "What is the cat's name?", 'options': ['Murka', 'Barsik', 'Kitty', 'Snowy'], 'correct': 'Murka'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What color is her fur?', 'sample': 'She has soft white fur with lovely black spots.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Where does Murka like to sleep all day?', 'options': ['On the floor', 'On the soft living room sofa', 'In the garden', 'Under the bed'], 'correct': 'On the soft living room sofa'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What does she chase in the evening?', 'sample': 'She chases a small red toy mouse across the wooden floor.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What does she drink from her ceramic bowl?', 'options': ['Water', 'Fresh milk', 'Juice', 'Tea'], 'correct': 'Fresh milk'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Where does she sleep at night?', 'sample': 'She sleeps at the foot of my bed at night.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What toy does she chase?', 'options': ['A red toy mouse', 'A ball', 'A string', 'A bird'], 'correct': 'A red toy mouse'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What color is her ceramic bowl?', 'sample': 'Her ceramic bowl is blue.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How is Murka described?', 'options': ['Cute and fluffy', 'Angry', 'Big', 'Loud'], 'correct': 'Cute and fluffy'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What does she do when someone strokes her head?', 'sample': 'She purrs loudly.'}]}]

READING_PASSAGES_A2 = [{'id': 'text_1', 'short_title': '1. 🌳 Поездка в деревню', 'title': 'Text 1: A Long Journey Through the Countryside', 'text': "Last summer, my best friend Mark and I decided to take a long and exciting trip away from the noisy, crowded city to explore the quiet and peaceful countryside. We spent a whole week planning our route, packing our backpacks with comfortable clothes, a large paper map, plenty of snacks, and a small digital camera to capture all the beautiful moments of our adventure. Early on a warm Saturday morning, we took a slow local train that traveled through green hills, small charming villages, and thick, mysterious forests. When we finally arrived at our destination, a lovely village named Green Valley, the air felt wonderfully fresh and clean compared to the heavy, polluted air of the big city.\n\nWe walked together from the small wooden train station to a cozy local guesthouse where we had booked a comfortable room for the weekend. The owners of the guesthouse, an elderly and very kind couple named Mr. and Mrs. Miller, welcomed us at the front door with warm smiles and a plate of freshly baked homemade apple pie. They sat with us in the kitchen for half an hour, telling us fascinating stories about the long history of the village, old local traditions, and the most secret, beautiful places to visit around the nearby blue lake. After a short rest in our room, we decided to take our very first walk along the narrow river path that started right behind the guesthouse garden.\n\nThe sun was shining brightly in the clear blue sky, and the weather was pleasantly warm, but a cool breeze was constantly blowing from the distant mountains. As we walked, we saw many domestic animals like cows and sheep eating green grass in the open fields, and colorful butterflies were flying around wild flowers growing by the path. Mark took many wonderful photographs of the landscape, while I stopped frequently to collect some interesting smooth stones near the water. Later in the evening, we returned to the guesthouse and enjoyed a delicious traditional dinner made from fresh local ingredients, including organic vegetables from the Millers' garden and fresh fish caught in the lake that morning.\n\nOn the second day of our trip, we woke up before sunrise to climb the highest hill in the area. The climb was quite difficult and made us very tired, but when we reached the top, the panoramic view was absolutely breathtaking. We could see the whole valley, the winding river, and the tiny houses of the village far below us. We sat on a large rock, ate our sandwiches, and drank hot tea from our thermoses while enjoying the absolute silence and beauty of nature. This unforgettable journey taught us to appreciate the simple things in life and gave us a lot of energy for our future work and studies back in the city.", 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Why did Mark and the narrator decide to take a trip?', 'options': ['To escape the noisy city', 'To visit a relative', 'To find a new job', 'To buy a house'], 'correct': 'To escape the noisy city'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: How did they travel to Green Valley?', 'sample': 'They traveled by a slow local train.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What was the name of the village they visited?', 'options': ['Green Valley', 'River Town', 'Mountain View', 'Sunny Hills'], 'correct': 'Green Valley'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Who welcomed them at the guesthouse?', 'options': ['A young couple', 'Mr. and Mrs. Miller', 'Their cousins', 'A local guide'], 'correct': 'Mr. and Mrs. Miller'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What did the owners give them upon arrival?', 'sample': 'They gave them freshly baked homemade apple pie.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What kind of animals did they see along the river path?', 'options': ['Lions and tigers', 'Cows and sheep', 'Horses and pigs', 'Monkeys and bears'], 'correct': 'Cows and sheep'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What did they do on the second day of their trip?', 'options': ['Stayed in bed', 'Climbed the highest hill', 'Visited a museum', 'Went swimming'], 'correct': 'Climbed the highest hill'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What did they drink from their thermoses on top of the hill?', 'sample': 'They drank hot tea from their thermoses.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What did this journey teach them?', 'options': ['To appreciate simple things in life', 'To hate the countryside', 'To buy a train', 'To cook pie'], 'correct': 'To appreciate simple things in life'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What did Mark take during the walk?', 'sample': 'Mark took many wonderful photographs of the landscape.'}]}, {'id': 'text_2', 'short_title': '2. ☕ День в кафе', 'title': 'Text 2: A Busy and Exciting Day at the Local Cafe', 'text': "Working at a popular cafe in the center of a busy town is never boring, and every single day brings new experiences, interesting people, and unexpected situations. My name is Jessica, and I have been working as a barista and waitress at 'The Golden Bean' cafe for almost two years now. My alarm clock always rings very early, at five o'clock in the morning, because our cafe opens its doors to the first customers at six o'clock sharp. I usually wash my face quickly, drink a glass of cold water, put on my neat black uniform, and walk briskly through the quiet morning streets before the town wakes up.\n\nWhen I arrive at the cafe, the first thing I do is unlock the heavy front door, turn on the bright lights, and switch on the big professional coffee machine. The machine needs about twenty minutes to warm up properly and reach the exact temperature needed to make the perfect espresso. While the machine is warming up, I prepare the front counter, check the display case filled with fresh croissants, chocolate muffins, and strawberry tarts, and write today's special menu on the large blackboard hanging near the entrance. Soon, the wonderful aroma of roasted coffee beans fills the entire room, making it feel warm and inviting.\n\nAt six o'clock, the first regular customers start arriving. Mr. Henderson, an old retired schoolteacher, is always our very first guest. He sits at the same corner table near the window every day, orders a strong black coffee with no sugar, and reads the morning newspaper from the first page to the last. A little later, groups of office workers and students rush in, looking sleepy and talking in a hurry while they wait for their takeaway lattes, cappuccinos, and breakfast sandwiches. During these busy morning hours, my hands move very quickly, and I have to remember multiple orders at the same time without writing them down, which requires a lot of concentration and practice.\n\nIn the afternoon, the atmosphere in the cafe changes completely. The rush is over, and the rooms become much quieter and more relaxed. Students come in to study for their exams, artists sit by the window drawing sketches in their notebooks, and old friends meet to chat for hours over a pot of green tea and a slice of cake. I really love this quiet part of my shift because I have time to talk to our guests, ask them how their day is going, and make sure everyone feels comfortable. Working here has helped me become much more confident, patient, and friendly when communicating with all kinds of different people.", 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': "What is the narrator's name?", 'options': ['Anna', 'Jessica', 'Sarah', 'Maria'], 'correct': 'Jessica'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What is the name of the cafe?', 'sample': 'The name of the cafe is The Golden Bean.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What time does her alarm clock ring?', 'options': ['At 4:00 AM', 'At 5:00 AM', 'At 6:00 AM', 'At 7:00 AM'], 'correct': 'At 5:00 AM'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How long does the coffee machine need to warm up?', 'options': ['10 minutes', '20 minutes', '30 minutes', '1 hour'], 'correct': '20 minutes'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Who is always the very first customer?', 'sample': 'Mr. Henderson, an old retired schoolteacher, is the first customer.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What does Mr. Henderson order every day?', 'options': ['Sweet tea', 'Strong black coffee with no sugar', 'Hot chocolate', 'Juice'], 'correct': 'Strong black coffee with no sugar'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What happens during the afternoon hours at the cafe?', 'options': ['It gets crowded', 'The atmosphere becomes quieter and more relaxed', 'Everyone leaves', 'They close'], 'correct': 'The atmosphere becomes quieter and more relaxed'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What do students do in the cafe in the afternoon?', 'sample': 'Students come in to study for their exams.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What has working at the cafe helped Jessica become?', 'options': ['More confident, patient, and friendly', 'Richer', 'Tired', 'A chef'], 'correct': 'More confident, patient, and friendly'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What does Jessica wear to work?', 'sample': 'She wears a neat black uniform.'}]}, {'id': 'text_3', 'short_title': '3. 👨\u200d👩\u200d👧\u200d👦 Семейный праздник', 'title': 'Text 3: Preparing for a Big Family Reunion', 'text': "Last month, my parents announced that our extended family was going to organize a massive family reunion to celebrate my grandparents' golden wedding anniversary. Fifty relatives from different parts of the country were planning to gather at our family house in the countryside, which meant we had a huge amount of preparation to do in just two weeks. Everyone in our household was assigned specific responsibilities to ensure everything would go smoothly and no important detail would be forgotten.\n\nMy mother took charge of the kitchen menu and grocery shopping, deciding to cook traditional dishes that our family had loved for generations. My father was responsible for cleaning the house, fixing the broken wooden fence in the backyard, and setting up a large white party tent on the lawn with plenty of tables and chairs. My younger sister and I were given the task of decorating the house and garden, creating photo collages from old family albums, and organizing funny games and music for both children and adults.\n\nThe days before the reunion were extremely exhausting. We spent hours washing windows, dusting rooms, polishing old silverware, and buying mountains of food at the local supermarket. On the Friday before the big event, my mother and aunts started cooking early in the morning, filling the house with the delicious smells of roasted chicken, garlic potatoes, freshly baked pies, and sweet fruit jams. My sister and I hung colorful paper lanterns and fairy lights around the garden trees so that the yard would look magical when the sun went down.\n\nOn Saturday afternoon, relatives started arriving in cars, buses, and trains. There were loud shouts of joy, warm hugs, happy tears, and endless talking as people who hadn't seen each other for years greeted one another. My grandparents looked so happy and moved when they saw everyone gathered together under one roof. We spent the entire evening eating wonderful food, listening to old stories about our family history, looking at funny childhood photos, and singing songs together. It was a tiring but truly wonderful weekend that reminded us how important family bonds really are in our fast-paced modern lives.", 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What event was the family preparing to celebrate?', 'options': ['Graduation', "Grandparents' golden wedding anniversary", 'Birthday', 'Wedding'], 'correct': "Grandparents' golden wedding anniversary"}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: How many relatives were planning to gather?', 'sample': 'Fifty relatives were planning to gather.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Where was the reunion taking place?', 'options': ['At a restaurant', 'At a hotel', 'At the family house in the countryside', 'In the city'], 'correct': 'At the family house in the countryside'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': "What was mother's responsibility?", 'options': ['Fixing the fence', 'Kitchen menu and grocery shopping', 'Decorating', 'Cleaning windows'], 'correct': 'Kitchen menu and grocery shopping'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What did father fix in the backyard?', 'sample': 'Father fixed the broken wooden fence.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What task did the narrator and sister given?', 'options': ['Decorating, creating photo collages, and organizing games', 'Cooking meat', 'Driving', 'Buying presents'], 'correct': 'Decorating, creating photo collages, and organizing games'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How did relatives arrive on Saturday afternoon?', 'options': ['By airplanes', 'By cars, buses, and trains', 'By bicycles', 'On foot'], 'correct': 'By cars, buses, and trains'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What did they hang around the garden trees?', 'sample': 'They hung colorful paper lanterns and fairy lights.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What did the weekend remind them of?', 'options': ['How important family bonds are', 'How hard work is', 'How expensive food is', 'How big the house is'], 'correct': 'How important family bonds are'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: How did grandparents look when everyone gathered?', 'sample': 'Grandparents looked very happy and moved.'}]}, {'id': 'text_4', 'short_title': '4. 🏰 Прогулка по Праге', 'title': 'Text 4: Exploring a Historic European City on Foot', 'text': 'During my autumn holidays last year, I traveled alone to Prague, a historic and magnificent European city known for its stunning architecture, cobblestone streets, and mysterious medieval legends. Instead of using public transport or joining large tourist groups, I decided to explore the entire city entirely on foot. I bought a comfortable pair of walking shoes, grabbed my small backpack with a water bottle and a guidebook, and stepped out onto the ancient streets early in the morning before the crowds woke up.\n\nWalking through the old town center felt like stepping back in time several centuries. The tall gothic churches, beautiful baroque palaces, and colorful old houses with red tile roofs created an atmosphere that was straight out of a fairy tale. I spent hours walking along the famous Charles Bridge, watching local street musicians play violin and guitar, looking at paintings made by local artists, and admiring the large stone statues standing proudly along both sides of the bridge against the misty morning sky.\n\nAs I continued walking, I discovered a hidden, quiet courtyard surrounded by tiny artisan shops selling handmade wooden toys, glass ornaments, and traditional local pastries. I stopped at a small open-air cafe tucked away in a quiet corner to try a traditional hot pastry filled with cinnamon and apples, accompanied by a cup of strong coffee. Sitting there, I watched local residents walk their dogs, children run around the old fountain, and pigeons gather around crumbs on the ancient cobblestones.\n\nIn the afternoon, I climbed up the steep hill leading to the massive Prague Castle, which overlooks the entire city and the winding Vltava river. From the top, the view of the golden towers and red roofs was simply breathtaking. Walking through this wonderful city on foot allowed me to notice small details that most tourists miss when they rush from one famous monument to another in a tour bus. It was an enriching experience that inspired me to learn more about European history and architecture.', 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Where did the narrator travel during autumn holidays?', 'options': ['Paris', 'Prague', 'Rome', 'London'], 'correct': 'Prague'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: How did the narrator explore the city?', 'sample': 'The narrator explored the city entirely on foot.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What can be found on the famous Charles Bridge?', 'options': ['Cars and buses', 'Street musicians, artists, and stone statues', 'A big market', 'A pool'], 'correct': 'Street musicians, artists, and stone statues'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What traditional pastry did the narrator try at a small cafe?', 'options': ['A pastry filled with cinnamon and apples', 'Chocolate croissant', 'Cake', 'Pie'], 'correct': 'A pastry filled with cinnamon and apples'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Where did the narrator go in the afternoon?', 'sample': 'The narrator climbed up the hill to Prague Castle.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What river flows through the city?', 'options': ['Thames', 'Seine', 'Vltava', 'Danube'], 'correct': 'Vltava'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Why was exploring on foot better according to the narrator?', 'options': ['It saved money', 'It allowed noticing small details', 'It was faster', 'It was easy'], 'correct': 'It allowed noticing small details'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What shoes did the narrator buy for the trip?', 'sample': 'The narrator bought a comfortable pair of walking shoes.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What architectural styles are mentioned in the old town?', 'options': ['Gothic and baroque', 'Modern and futuristic', 'Minimalist', 'Classical only'], 'correct': 'Gothic and baroque'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What did local residents do near the cafe?', 'sample': 'Local residents walked their dogs near the cafe.'}]}, {'id': 'text_5', 'short_title': '5. 🗝 Тайны старого дома', 'title': 'Text 5: Discovering the Secrets of an Old Country House', 'text': "Every summer when I was a little child, my parents used to send me to spend July and August at my grandparents' old country house, which was located near a quiet forest far away from any major town. The house was very old, built more than a hundred years ago by my great-grandfather, and it was full of creaking wooden floors, mysterious dark corners, high ceilings, and walls covered with framed black-and-white photographs of our ancestors. To a young child, that house felt like a giant castle full of endless secrets waiting to be discovered.\n\nMy favorite place in the entire house was the dusty, mysterious attic under the roof. My grandmother usually told me not to go up there alone because of the old furniture and dust, but whenever she was busy gardening, I loved sneaking up the narrow wooden stairs to explore. The attic was lit by a single small round window that let in beams of golden sunlight filled with dancing dust particles. There were old wooden boxes, broken chairs, heavy winter coats, and large leather suitcases covered with colorful travel stickers from countries I had never heard of before.\n\nOne rainy afternoon, while searching through a heavy wooden chest in the darkest corner of the attic, I found something truly amazing: a heavy metal box filled with old childhood toys, comic books from the 1950s, a collection of shiny foreign coins, and a handwritten diary belonging to my grandfather when he was a boy of my age. When my grandfather found me reading it later that evening, he didn't get angry at all; instead, he smiled gently, sat down next to me on the old sofa, and spent two hours telling me wonderful stories about his childhood adventures in those same woods.\n\nYears have passed since then, and my grandparents are no longer with us, but that old country house still belongs to our family. Whenever I feel tired or stressed by modern city life, I visit the house, walk through the quiet rooms, and remember those golden summer days. It always brings a deep sense of peace, warmth, and connection to my family roots.", 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Where did the narrator spend July and August as a child?', 'options': ['At a hotel', "At grandparents' old country house", 'At camp', 'In the city'], 'correct': "At grandparents' old country house"}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Who built the house more than a hundred years ago?', 'sample': 'The great-grandfather built the house.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': "What was the narrator's favorite place in the house?", 'options': ['The kitchen', 'The attic under the roof', 'The basement', 'The garden'], 'correct': 'The attic under the roof'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What did grandmother usually tell the narrator?', 'options': ['Not to go up to the attic alone', 'To clean the attic', 'To sleep there', 'To invite friends'], 'correct': 'Not to go up to the attic alone'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What let light into the attic?', 'sample': 'A single small round window let light into the attic.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Whose diary was found in the metal box?', 'options': ["Grandmother's", "Father's", "Grandfather's when he was a boy", "Great-grandfather's"], 'correct': "Grandfather's when he was a boy"}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How did grandfather react when he found the narrator reading it?', 'options': ['He got angry', 'He smiled gently and told stories', 'He took the box', 'He punished him'], 'correct': 'He smiled gently and told stories'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What was in the heavy metal box?', 'sample': 'The box had old toys, comics, foreign coins, and a diary.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What does visiting the house bring to the narrator now?', 'options': ['Stress', 'A deep sense of peace, warmth, and connection to roots', 'Boredom', 'Fear'], 'correct': 'A deep sense of peace, warmth, and connection to roots'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: When does the narrator visit the house now?', 'sample': 'The narrator visits when feeling tired or stressed by city life.'}]}, {'id': 'text_6', 'short_title': '6. 🐾 Помощь в приюте', 'title': 'Text 6: Volunteering at the Local Animal Shelter', 'text': "Every Saturday morning, sixteen-year-old Leo wakes up much earlier than on school days because he has a very important and special job to do. For the past six months, Leo has been volunteering as a helper at 'Happy Paws', the largest animal rescue shelter in his town. He has always loved animals more than anything else in the world, and ever since his parents refused to let him keep a large dog in their small apartment, he decided that helping shelter animals was the best way to share his love and care with pets that really need a second chance in life.\n\nWhen Leo arrives at the shelter at eight o'clock in the morning, the director, an energetic woman named Mrs. Davis, greets him with a warm smile and gives him a list of daily tasks. The first and most important task is always feeding the dogs and cats. Leo carefully measures out the right amount of food and fresh water for each animal, paying special attention to older dogs who need special soft food and medicine. After feeding time, he spends an hour cleaning the outdoor play yards and washing food bowls to keep everything perfectly clean, safe, and comfortable for the animals.\n\nThe best part of Leo's volunteer shift always begins at ten o'clock when it is time for exercise and socialization. Leo takes dogs of different sizes and breeds for long, energetic walks along the quiet forest paths behind the shelter. He loves watching energetic puppies run around, chase tennis balls, and wag their tails happily in the sunshine. For the cats who stay indoors, Leo sits on the floor with colorful toys, feathers, and balls of yarn, helping shy kittens learn to trust humans again so they can find loving families much faster.\n\nVolunteering at the animal shelter has taught Leo a lot of valuable life lessons about responsibility, patience, empathy, and hard work. Although sometimes it makes him feel sad to see abandoned pets, the feeling of joy he gets when a rescued dog finds a new home and a caring owner makes all his hard work completely worthwhile. He encourages all his school friends to spend a few hours helping animals instead of playing video games all weekend long.", 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How old is Leo?', 'options': ['14', '15', '16', '18'], 'correct': '16'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What is the name of the animal shelter?', 'sample': 'The shelter is named Happy Paws.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Why did Leo choose to volunteer?', 'options': ['To earn money', "His parents wouldn't let him keep a large dog at home", 'School credits', 'Free pets'], 'correct': "His parents wouldn't let him keep a large dog at home"}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Who is the director of the shelter?', 'options': ['Mrs. Smith', 'Mrs. Davis', 'Mr. Brown', 'Miss White'], 'correct': 'Mrs. Davis'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': "Write a short sentence: What is Leo's first morning task?", 'sample': 'His first task is feeding the dogs and cats.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'When does exercise and socialization begin?', 'options': ['8:00 AM', '9:00 AM', '10:00 AM', '12:00 PM'], 'correct': '10:00 AM'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What does Leo use to play with indoor cats?', 'options': ['Colorful toys, feathers, and balls of yarn', 'Sticks', 'Lasers', 'Boxes'], 'correct': 'Colorful toys, feathers, and balls of yarn'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What life lessons has volunteering taught Leo?', 'sample': 'It taught him responsibility, patience, empathy, and hard work.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What does Leo encourage his school friends to do?', 'options': ['Spend hours helping animals instead of playing video games', 'Study more', 'Play sports', 'Work in a cafe'], 'correct': 'Spend hours helping animals instead of playing video games'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What time does Leo arrive at the shelter?', 'sample': "Leo arrives at the shelter at eight o'clock in the morning."}]}, {'id': 'text_7', 'short_title': '7. 🎸 Уроки гитары', 'title': 'Text 7: Discovering the Joy of Playing the Guitar', 'text': 'For many years, Kevin dreamed of learning how to play a musical instrument, but he always believed that he was simply not talented enough to master something as complex as the guitar. Everything changed on his fourteenth birthday when his uncle, who is a professional jazz musician, gave him an old acoustic guitar that had been kept in a wooden case for over twenty years. The guitar had a few minor scratches on its wooden body and needed new steel strings, but to Kevin, it looked like the most valuable and magical treasure in the world.\n\nThe following day, Kevin started watching free video tutorials on YouTube, trying to understand how to hold the instrument correctly, how to use a guitar pick, and how to press his fingers firmly against the metal frets. His very first practice sessions were quite frustrating and painful. Pressing the thin strings with bare fingers hurt his hand muscles, and his fingers developed sore red spots that made writing at school a little difficult. His early attempts to play basic chords like C major and G major sounded clumsy, buzzing, and completely out of tune.\n\nHowever, Kevin refused to give up easily. He decided to practice for just twenty minutes every single day after finishing his homework, following a strict routine. Slowly, after two weeks of steady practice, the pain in his fingers disappeared as small calluses formed on his skin. The chords started sounding clean and clear, and he was able to change from one chord to another without stopping. His family members were very surprised when they heard him play a simple melody for the very first time in the living room.\n\nNow, six months later, Kevin can play twenty of his favorite songs and often performs acoustic tunes for his friends when they gather around a campfire on summer evenings. Learning the guitar taught him that natural talent is much less important than daily practice, patience, and a strong desire to achieve your personal goals. He is already planning to write his own original song next month.', 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Who gave Kevin his first guitar?', 'options': ['His father', 'His teacher', 'His uncle', 'His friend'], 'correct': 'His uncle'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: On what occasion did he receive the guitar?', 'sample': 'He received it on his fourteenth birthday.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Where did Kevin find free video tutorials?', 'options': ['Television', 'YouTube', 'DVD', 'School'], 'correct': 'YouTube'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Why were his first practice sessions painful?', 'options': ['Guitar was too big', 'Pressing thin strings hurt his bare fingers', 'Too loud', 'Hand injury'], 'correct': 'Pressing thin strings hurt his bare fingers'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: How long did Kevin practice every day?', 'sample': 'He practiced for twenty minutes every single day.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How many songs can Kevin play after six months?', 'options': ['5', '10', '20', '50'], 'correct': '20'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What did learning the guitar teach Kevin?', 'options': ['Daily practice is more important than natural talent', 'Music is easy', 'Guitars are cheap', 'Uncles are wise'], 'correct': 'Daily practice is more important than natural talent'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What is Kevin planning to do next month?', 'sample': 'He is planning to write his own original song.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': "What profession does Kevin's uncle have?", 'options': ['Professional jazz musician', 'Teacher', 'Carpenter', 'Artist'], 'correct': 'Professional jazz musician'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Where does Kevin perform acoustic tunes for friends?', 'sample': 'He performs for friends when they gather around a campfire.'}]}, {'id': 'text_8', 'short_title': '8. 🌱 Огород на дворе', 'title': 'Text 8: Learning How to Grow a Vegetable Garden', 'text': "Last spring, Anna and her younger brother Tom decided to transform a neglected patch of grass in their backyard into a productive and colorful organic vegetable garden. Neither of them had any prior gardening experience, so they borrowed thick instruction books from the local library, watched educational gardening videos online, and asked their grandmother, who had grown vegetables all her life, for practical advice and helpful tips.\n\nTheir first big challenge was clearing away the thick weeds, large stones, and hard dry soil using heavy shovels and rakes. It was exhausting physical work under the warm sun, but they worked together for two entire weekends until the ground was soft, dark, and ready for planting. Next, they mixed rich compost into the soil to give the future plants all the necessary nutrients they would need to grow healthy, strong, and delicious.\n\nThey carefully chose a variety of easy-to-grow vegetables that thrive in their local climate, including juicy red tomatoes, crunchy orange carrots, crisp green lettuce, sweet strawberries, and aromatic basil. Anna planted the tiny seeds in neat rows while Tom made small wooden signs with the names of each vegetable so they wouldn't mix them up. Every single morning before going to school, they took turns watering the garden carefully with a long green hose, making sure the young plants didn't dry out.\n\nAfter a few weeks of waiting patiently, the first tiny green sprouts finally emerged from the dark soil, bringing enormous excitement to the brother and sister. Throughout the summer months, they watched their garden grow taller and greener every day, pulling out weeds and protecting the plants from insects. By late July, they harvested their very first crop of fresh salad ingredients. Eating a dinner made from vegetables they grew with their own hands was an incredible feeling of pride and satisfaction for both of them.", 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Who decided to start a vegetable garden?', 'options': ['Anna and Tom', 'Anna and grandmother', 'Tom and friend', 'Parents'], 'correct': 'Anna and Tom'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: When did they start the garden project?', 'sample': 'They started the project last spring.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What was their first big challenge?', 'options': ['Building a fence', 'Clearing away weeds, stones, and hard soil', 'Buying seeds', 'Digging a well'], 'correct': 'Clearing away weeds, stones, and hard soil'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What did they mix into the soil?', 'options': ['Sand', 'Rich compost', 'Stones', 'Plastic'], 'correct': 'Rich compost'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What did Tom make after Anna planted seeds?', 'sample': 'Tom made small wooden signs with the vegetable names.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'When did they harvest their very first crop?', 'options': ['By late July', 'In May', 'On Halloween', 'In September'], 'correct': 'By late July'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How long did the clearing work take them?', 'options': ['Two entire weekends', 'One day', 'A month', 'Five hours'], 'correct': 'Two entire weekends'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: How did they water the garden every morning?', 'sample': 'They watered the garden with a long green hose.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What feelings did eating their own vegetables bring?', 'options': ['Pride and satisfaction', 'Disappointment', 'Boredom', 'Hunger'], 'correct': 'Pride and satisfaction'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Where did they borrow thick instruction books?', 'sample': 'They borrowed instruction books from the local library.'}]}, {'id': 'text_9', 'short_title': '9. 🚆 Путешествие на поезде', 'title': 'Text 9: A Memorable Train Journey Across the Country', 'text': 'When most people plan a long journey across the country, they usually choose to travel by airplane because it is fast, modern, and saves a lot of time. However, last autumn, Oliver decided to do something completely different and booked a twelve-hour ticket on a traditional cross-country passenger train. He wanted to escape the stressful airport security lines, cramped airplane seats, and rushing crowds, preferring to enjoy a slower, more peaceful way of traveling while watching the landscape change outside his window.\n\nOn the morning of his trip, Oliver arrived at the historic central railway station with a large suitcase, a good detective novel, a notebook, and a thermos filled with hot homemade coffee. He found his comfortable seat by the large window in a clean passenger carriage just ten minutes before departure. When the heavy train slowly began to move away from the platform, he smiled, opened his book, and prepared for a long day of relaxation and quiet observation.\n\nThe train route passed through places that are completely invisible from modern highways and airplane windows. For hours, Oliver watched golden autumn forests, wide rushing rivers, quiet agricultural farms with grazing horses, and small sleepy villages where time seemed to move much slower than in the city. During short stops at small country stations, local passengers carrying baskets of fresh apples and homemade bread boarded the train, adding a wonderful local atmosphere to the journey.\n\nIn the afternoon, Oliver walked down the corridor to the dining car, where he met a friendly elderly painter who was traveling to the mountains to find inspiration for his new artwork. They spent over an hour drinking tea and talking about art, travel, life experiences, and favorite books while the scenery rushed past the windows. When the train finally reached its destination late in the evening, Oliver felt completely rested and inspired, realizing that sometimes the journey itself can be much more enjoyable and memorable than the final destination.', 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Why do most people usually travel by airplane?', 'options': ["Because it's fast and modern", 'Cheap', 'Comfortable', 'Views'], 'correct': "Because it's fast and modern"}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What ticket did Oliver book last autumn?', 'sample': 'Oliver booked a twelve-hour train ticket.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': "Where was Oliver's seat located?", 'options': ['Near the door', 'By the large window', 'In the dining car', 'Next to conductor'], 'correct': 'By the large window'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What did local passengers carry at station stops?', 'options': ['Backpacks', 'Baskets of fresh apples and homemade bread', 'Money', 'Flowers'], 'correct': 'Baskets of fresh apples and homemade bread'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Whom did Oliver meet in the dining car?', 'sample': 'Oliver met a friendly elderly painter in the dining car.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What did Oliver realize by the end of the trip?', 'options': ['Trains are slow', 'The journey itself can be more enjoyable than the destination', 'Airplanes are better', 'Traveling is tiring'], 'correct': 'The journey itself can be more enjoyable than the destination'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What did Oliver bring with him to drink?', 'options': ['Tea', 'A thermos filled with hot homemade coffee', 'Juice', 'Water'], 'correct': 'A thermos filled with hot homemade coffee'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What book did Oliver bring?', 'sample': 'Oliver brought a good detective novel.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What season was it during his journey?', 'options': ['Spring', 'Summer', 'Autumn', 'Winter'], 'correct': 'Autumn'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: How did Oliver feel when the train reached its destination?', 'sample': 'Oliver felt completely rested and inspired.'}]}, {'id': 'text_10', 'short_title': '10. 🪵 Домик на дереве', 'title': 'Text 10: Building a Homemade Treehouse', 'text': "Ever since they read an adventure book about pirates and secret hideouts, ten-year-old Lucas and his cousin Max dreamed of having their own treehouse high up in the branches of the old oak tree in their grandparents' backyard. For months, they drew countless colorful sketches on paper, measured wooden planks in the garage, and begged their parents and grandfather to help them turn their ambitious architectural dream into reality.\n\nTheir grandfather, who was a retired carpenter with decades of experience, agreed to supervise the project on condition that safety would always come first. He taught the boys how to measure accurately, how to use hand tools properly, and why strong support beams were necessary to hold the weight of the wooden platform. They spent three full weekends working hard outdoors, sawing wood, hammering large steel nails, and sanding rough wooden surfaces so nobody would get splinters while playing.\n\nBuilding the walls and the small slanted roof was the most difficult part of the construction process, requiring a lot of teamwork, patience, and careful balancing on tall ladders. Max painted the exterior walls in a nice forest green color so the treehouse would blend nicely with the leaves, while Lucas made a sturdy rope ladder to reach the entrance safely. They even decorated the interior with old cushions, a small wooden table, comic books, and a flag they designed themselves.\n\nWhen the treehouse was finally finished on a sunny Sunday afternoon, the cousins celebrated by having a picnic inside their new secret headquarters, looking down at the backyard from the high branches. It became their favorite place to read adventure stories, play board games, and talk about their dreams during the long summer holidays. Working on this project taught them valuable practical skills and brought them much closer together as best friends.", 'questions': [{'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What inspired Lucas and Max to build a treehouse?', 'options': ['Space movie', 'An adventure book about pirates and secret hideouts', 'School project', 'Game'], 'correct': 'An adventure book about pirates and secret hideouts'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: Whose backyard was chosen?', 'sample': "Their grandparents' backyard was chosen."}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What kind of tree was used?', 'options': ['Oak tree', 'Pine tree', 'Apple tree', 'Birch tree'], 'correct': 'Oak tree'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'Who supervised the construction project?', 'options': ['Father', 'Grandfather, a retired carpenter', 'Uncle', 'Architect'], 'correct': 'Grandfather, a retired carpenter'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': "Write a short sentence: What was grandfather's main condition?", 'sample': 'His main condition was that safety would always come first.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How long did they spend working outdoors?', 'options': ['Three full weekends', 'One week', 'Two months', 'Five days'], 'correct': 'Three full weekends'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'What color did Max paint the exterior walls?', 'options': ['Red', 'Blue', 'Forest green', 'Yellow'], 'correct': 'Forest green'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: How do they reach the entrance safely?', 'sample': 'They use a sturdy rope ladder.'}, {'type': 'choice', 'question': 'How did they celebrate finishing the treehouse?', 'options': ['Having a picnic inside', 'Sleeping overnight', 'Inviting the town', 'Painting it again'], 'correct': 'Having a picnic inside'}, {'type': 'open', 'question': 'Write a short sentence: What did working on the project teach them?', 'sample': 'It taught them valuable practical skills and brought them closer together.'}]}]